---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<Layout
  title="Experience"
  description="Naman Patel’s hands-on experience across SEO, content, web products, Android, AI-assisted development, automation, QA, and release workflows."
>
  <div class="editorial-page experience-editorial">
    <section class="page-hero shell shell--wide" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
      <div class="experience-intro-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="page-kicker">Experience / built, broken, shipped</p>
          <h1 id="experience-title">The skills only make sense when they <span class="accent-blue">connect.</span></h1>
          <p class="page-lede">Search was the entry point. Then the work kept pulling me into publishing, product, code, AI-assisted workflows, Android, QA, automation, and releases.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="action-dark" href={`${base}projects/`}>See what I’ve built <span>→</span></a>
            <a class="action-light" href="https://github.com/namanlabc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="experience-note">
          I’m largely self-taught. I care less about collecting tool names than being able to move from a messy problem to something useful, measurable, tested, and actually live.
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap shell shell--wide" aria-labelledby="lanes-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">01 / THE WORK TRAIL</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="lanes-title">One problem kept leading to the next skill.</h2>
          <p>The useful part is not each box by itself. It is being able to carry context across the whole path from research to release.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-lanes">
        <article class="experience-lane">
          <span class="experience-lane__num">01</span>
          <div>
            <p class="micro-label">SEARCH → CONTENT → MEASUREMENT</p>
            <h3>SEO taught me to start with what people actually need.</h3>
            <p>Keyword research, search intent, content structure, on-page work, WordPress publishing, technical cleanup, Search Console, analytics, and diagnosing why a page stopped working.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="lane-tools" aria-label="SEO skills and tools">
            <span>Search Console</span><span>Search intent</span><span>Technical SEO</span><span>WordPress</span><span>Schema</span><span>Analytics</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="experience-lane">
          <span class="experience-lane__num">02</span>
          <div>
            <p class="micro-label">IDEA → INTERFACE → CODE → DEPLOY</p>
            <h3>Eventually I wanted to build the thing, not only grow it.</h3>
            <p>That pushed me into Astro, HTML, CSS, responsive interfaces, GitHub, debugging, deployment, and product decisions. I like getting a rough idea far enough that somebody else can open it and immediately understand what to do.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="lane-tools" aria-label="Product and web skills">
            <span>Astro</span><span>HTML / CSS / JS</span><span>Tailwind</span><span>Git</span><span>GitHub</span><span>Deployments</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="experience-lane">
          <span class="experience-lane__num">03</span>
          <div>
            <p class="micro-label">ISSUE → AGENTS → BUILD → QA → RELEASE</p>
            <h3>Now the work crosses AI, Android, automation, QA, and releases.</h3>
            <p>I use AI coding tools as part of a supervised build loop, alongside Android Studio, Kotlin, Gradle, GitHub workflows, emulator testing, build artifacts, and release checks. Speed is useful only if the output survives verification.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="lane-tools" aria-label="AI, Android and workflow skills">
            <span>Codex</span><span>Claude</span><span>OpenCode</span><span>OpenRouter</span><span>Kotlin</span><span>Android Studio</span><span>Gradle</span><span>GitHub Actions</span><span>QA</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap hairline-top" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
      <div class="shell shell--wide">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-kicker">02 / RECEIPTS</p>
          <div>
            <h2 id="evidence-title">Real work is where the lessons stuck.</h2>
            <p>Traffic, users, technical failures, and release pressure are much better teachers than a neat list of certifications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-strip">
          <article>
            <p class="micro-label">CONTENT PROJECT</p>
            <strong>~1M</strong>
            <h3>monthly visitors at peak</h3>
            <p>One of my own content projects grew to roughly a million monthly visitors at its peak.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <p class="micro-label">OUTCOME</p>
            <strong>Acquired</strong>
            <h3>entertainment project</h3>
            <p>A US-focused entertainment site I worked on was later acquired by WealthOfGeeks Media.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <p class="micro-label">CURRENT LAB</p>
            <strong>Shipping</strong>
            <h3>products + tooling</h3>
            <p>SmallMB, Astro SEO Audit, Get Random Letter, and newer experiments are where the next layer gets tested.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-wrap shell shell--wide" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="section-kicker">03 / WORKING STACK</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="stack-title">Tools are useful when they disappear into the workflow.</h2>
          <p>I do not care about displaying every logo I have ever opened. These are the groups I actually move between while making things.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stack-lines">
        <div class="stack-line"><span>Search / publish</span><p>Search Console · WordPress · technical SEO · content systems · HTML · CSS</p></div>
        <div class="stack-line"><span>Build / ship</span><p>Astro · Tailwind · Git · GitHub · deployment · debugging</p></div>
        <div class="stack-line"><span>Android / QA</span><p>Kotlin · Android Studio · Gradle · emulator testing · smoke checks · release artifacts</p></div>
        <div class="stack-line"><span>AI / agents</span><p>Codex · Claude · OpenCode · OpenRouter · model routing · supervised agent workflows</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a class="action-dark" href={`${base}projects/`}>Projects <span>→</span></a>
        <a class="action-light" href={`${base}about/`}>More about me <span>→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>